SkyArena
========

An 8-bit interactive sky built from open data, made with AI-assisted workflows
in VS Code with GitHub Copilot. Copyright for the original code, runners, and
prompt files is in LICENSE (MIT).

Third-party notices
-------------------

Python
    Host and repo .venv interpreter (3.11+). PSF License.
    https://docs.python.org/3/license.html

Git
    Version control. GPL-2.0.
    https://git-scm.com/

Visual Studio Code and GitHub Copilot
    Editor and AI assistant used to build this piece. The fly-* prompt files
    under .github/prompts/ are project customizations for Copilot Chat.
    Proprietary. https://code.visualstudio.com/
    https://github.com/features/copilot

OpenRouter
    Routes the model calls used in the AI part of the workshop. The API key
    is supplied to each participant and stored in a gitignored .env.
    https://openrouter.ai/

idtracker.ai
    Multi-animal tracking used for the Drosophila and zebrafish CSVs.
    GPL-3.0. https://idtracker.ai/
    Torrents J, Costa T, de Polavieja GG. 2026. New idtracker.ai
    rethinks multi-animal tracking as a representation learning
    problem to increase accuracy and reduce tracking time. eLife
    14:RP107602. doi:10.7554/eLife.107602.4
    https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.107602.4
    Drive (anyone-with-link validated CSVs):
    https://drive.google.com/file/d/17Cn8rT8Fk9QLcAnU8yokScMdqTk8QA5u/view
    https://drive.google.com/file/d/1eVZWK89DHTkyQNL5B0Euj9ezGvqzTvyl/view

Tao et al. 2019
    Statistical structure of locomotion (v||, v-perp HMM/HHMM). The fly
    tracks follow that observation model in the standard library; this is
    not a MATLAB port.
    eLife 8:e41235. doi:10.7554/eLife.41235
    https://elifesciences.org/articles/41235
    https://github.com/bhandawat/HHMM (GPL-3.0)

Dommanget-Kott et al. 2024
    Hidden Markov model of zebrafish locomotion. The fish tracks cite this
    and use the same standard-library sampler as the flies.
    doi:10.1101/2024.11.22.624881
    https://www.biorxiv.org/content/10.1101/2024.11.22.624881

EMSC / SeismicPortal
    Earthquake catalogue for 2026-06-21, all magnitudes, via the FDSN event
    service. Curated to data/curated/quakes_21062026.json.
    https://www.seismicportal.eu/
    https://www.seismicportal.eu/fdsnws/event/1/query

Hoffleit D., Warren Jr W.H. 1991
    Bright Star Catalogue, 5th Revised Ed. CDS V/50. Downloaded as ReadMe
    and catalog.gz, curated to data/curated/stars_catalog.
    https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/ftp/cats/V/50/
    https://vizier.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/VizieR?-source=V/50

pyarrow
    Apache Arrow Python library. Writes fly.parquet and fish.parquet.
    Apache-2.0. Installed into the repo .venv only.
    https://arrow.apache.org/

gdown
    Drive fallback when Google returns an HTML interstitial. MIT. Installed
    into the repo .venv only when needed.
    https://github.com/wkentaro/gdown

Pillow
    Imaging library used by app/utils/sprites/organic_sprites.py and
    cyber_sprites.py to draw the sprite PNG frames. It is not needed to run
    the piece. HPND-Pillow. Install it into the repo .venv only if you redraw
    the sprites.
    https://python-pillow.org/

Press Start 2P
    Pixel font shipped in app/fonts/, used for the title screen and the HUD
    text. SIL Open Font License 1.1 (app/fonts/OFL.txt). Copyright 2012 The
    Press Start 2P Project Authors.
    https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Press+Start+2P

Animal sprites
    15x15 (fly) and 19x19 (fish) grow, flicker, and shrink PNG frames under
    app/utils/sprites/fly and fish, in an east-facing and a down-right version
    (n.png and n_d.png). Drawn by organic_sprites.py in that folder from
    shapes, in the colors of app/palette.js. A neon set is kept beside them in
    cyber-fly and cyber-fish. MIT with the rest of this repo. Served from that
    folder, PNG only.

World capitals
    Country capital coordinates shipped in data/raw/capitals/locations.json
    and curated to data/curated/capitals.json.
